# Design tokens

**When:** introducing or changing visual variables (type, color, space, radius, shadow, breakpoints, dark theme) under `web/`.

## Precedence (required)

1. **Use existing CSS custom properties** from `web/src/app/styles/tokens/`:
   - `app-design-tokens-foundation.css` — spacing, type ramp, motion, breakpoints, layout, z-index
   - `app-design-tokens-light.css` — light surfaces, borders, text, brand, semantic colors, shadows
   - `app-design-tokens-dark.css` — dark theme overrides
2. **Prefer composition** of current components / classes already in `web/`.
3. **Only then** use numeric/CSS defaults below — labeled **fallback when no token exists**. Never hardcode a hex/`rgba` in component CSS if a `--*` token already exists. Invent a new token only when none fit; add it in the tokens files, not inline.

Repo chrome already defines product colors, type ramp (capped sizes), spacing, radius, shadows, and motion. Do not re-author a rival Stripe-ish palette that fights foundation/light/dark.

---

## Typography

### Hierarchy

- Use a **maximum of 3 type sizes** per view (product ramp is capped further in foundation tokens).
- Establish clear hierarchy: **Display → Heading → Body → Caption/Label**
- Never let body text compete with headings visually.

### Rules

- Prefer product fonts from tokens (`--font-sans`, `--font-mono`) over inventing stacks.
- **Never use more than 2 typefaces** in a single product.
- Body text minimum: `15px` equivalent (check `--text-*`); caption never below `12px` / `--text-xs` floor in CI.
- Line length: prefer `--layout-readable-max` / ~`60–75ch` for prose. Never let prose stretch full-width.
- Avoid center-aligned body text. Left-align for readability.
- Headings: `font-weight: 600–700`. Body: `400–450`. Labels: `500`.
- Use `rem` for typography — not raw `px`.

### Fallback type scale (when no token exists)

```css
--text-xs:    0.75rem;   /* 12px */
--text-sm:    0.875rem;  /* 14px */
--text-base:  0.9375rem; /* 15px */
--text-md:    1rem;      /* 16px */
--text-lg:    1.125rem;  /* 18px */
--text-xl:    1.25rem;   /* 20px */
--text-2xl:   1.5rem;    /* 24px */
```

Prefer foundation aliases (`--text-sm`, `--text-md`, `--text-title-app`, …) over inventing new steps.

---

## Color

- Color communicates **meaning**, not decoration.
- One primary action color; semantic colors for status — never repurpose brand for errors/success.
- Interactive elements: consistent color that signals clickability.
- Backgrounds: subtle tonal shifts via tokens, not hard borders alone.
- **Never use pure `#000000` or `#ffffff`** for body text/bg when near-black/warm-white tokens exist.
- Contrast: body **4.5:1** (AA); large text **3:1**; UI/focus **3:1**; aim **7:1** where possible.

### Fallback palette (when no token exists)

Only if foundation/light/dark have no suitable `--color-*`. Prefer adding to light/dark token files over pasting these hexes into components.

```css
--color-bg:             #ffffff;
--color-bg-subtle:      #f6f8fa;
--color-border:         rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
--color-text-primary:   #0a0a0a;
--color-text-secondary: #4b5563;
--color-success:        #00a96e;
--color-warning:        #f59e0b;
--color-error:          #ef4444;
--color-info:           #3b82f6;
```

---

## Spacing & layout

- All spacing multiples of **4px** / tokens `--space-*`.
- Max content: prefer `--layout-max-width`; prose/forms often tighter (`--layout-readable-max`).
- Group related elements closer than unrelated ones (Gestalt proximity).
- **Never center a layout that should be left-aligned** (forms, settings, text).
- Use **12-column** mental grid at desktop, **4-column** at mobile; collapse multi-column below `--bp-md`.

### Fallback spacing (when no token exists)

```css
--space-1: 0.25rem; /* 4px */  --space-2: 0.5rem;  --space-3: 0.75rem;
--space-4: 1rem;    --space-6: 1.5rem; --space-8: 2rem;
--space-12: 3rem;   --space-16: 4rem;
```

---

## Border radius

Use `--radius-*` from tokens. Consistency is critical: pick the scale and do not deviate.

| Use | Token (preferred) | Fallback if missing |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Inputs, tags | `--radius-sm` / `--radius-md` | `4px` / `8px` |
| Buttons | `--radius-md` | `8px` (not fully round unless pill) |
| Cards, panels | `--radius-lg` / `--radius-xl` | `12px` / `16px` |
| Modals | `--radius-xl` | `16px` |
| Pills, avatars | `--radius-full` | `9999px` |

---

## Shadows & elevation

Prefer light/dark shadow tokens. Cards in this product often use **border, not shadow** — match existing chrome.

| Level | Role |
| --- | --- |
| 0 | Flat — base page, sidebars |
| 1 | Cards / row hover (`shadow-sm`) when elevation is used |
| 2 | Dropdowns, popovers |
| 3 | Modals, drawers |
| 4 | Floating actions / command palette |

Never mix elevation levels in the same component cluster. Focus: `var(--shadow-focus)` or equivalent — never bare `outline: none`.

### Fallback shadows (when no token exists)

```css
--shadow-sm: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.06), 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
--shadow-md: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0,0,0,0.06), 0 2px 4px -1px rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
--shadow-lg: 0 10px 15px -3px rgba(0,0,0,0.07), 0 4px 6px -2px rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
--shadow-focus: 0 0 0 3px rgba(99,91,255,0.35); /* replace with brand token tint */
```

---

## Dark mode & responsive tokens

- Support `prefers-color-scheme` / `[data-theme="dark"]` patterns already in token files — do not invent a second theme map.
- Never simply invert colors; redesign luminance and borders for dark context.
- Shadows are weaker in dark mode — prefer border / subtle glow tokens already defined.
- Breakpoints: use `--bp-*` from foundation. **Mobile-first.**

### Fallback breakpoints (when no token exists)

```css
--bp-sm: 640px; --bp-md: 768px; --bp-lg: 1024px; --bp-xl: 1280px;
```

---

## Consistency

- **Color:** only design-token variables in components — no hardcoded hex.
- **Spacing:** 4px grid via `--space-*`.
- **Icons:** one icon set; default ~`18px`/`20px`.
- **Density:** compact / default / spacious — pick one per context.

---

## Do not

- Duplicate a second brand palette alongside `tokens/*`.
- Hardcode hex in component CSS when a `--*` exists.
- Use `px` for type scale in new rules — use `rem` / tokens.
- Mix border + shadow as the same card affordance — pick one (product prefers border).
